---
source: crates/surfaces/cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Set a field (or --title) of an entity

Usage: specforge set [OPTIONS] <ENTITY> [FIELD] [VALUES]...

Arguments:
  <ENTITY>
          The entity to change

  [FIELD]
          The field, or `field.entry` for one entry of a block field

  [VALUES]...
          The value; a list field takes several (a reference list also one separated by commas)

Options:
      --title <TITLE>
          Change the header title instead of a field

      --annotation <NAME[=VALUE]>
          An annotation to write after the value (`readonly`, `since=1.2`); replaces the field's

      --dry-run
          Print the diff and write nothing

      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

  -h, --help
          Print help
